# memory_gap_partial_range: A memory map whose only range ends 8 KiB into its last 16 KiB page. In the map setup the range is used as given: a command buffer in the page's first half is read (a copy through the memory map) and runs, and a buffer over that page cannot be mapped (the range covers half of it: "Incomplete range"), so its exec faults. In the isolate setup no isolated task is made: the range is not whole pages, which an isolated task needs, so the define faults, and so does every later command for the task ("Invalid task"). Map and isolate setups only: the blocks setup has no memory map.
